{
  "$comment": [
    "GoMesh publishes on meshcore/<CODE>/<pubkey>/<stream>, where <CODE> is the",
    "airport identifier of the uplink gateway's metro - NOT the node's own position.",
    "Use it only as a coarse hint for observers that never publish coordinates.",
    "A code absent from BOTH blocks is currently left unclassified: its observers stay",
    "listed with no region and the code is logged once. Absent does NOT mean excluded.",
    "Only the outOfArea block excludes.",
    "confidence=observed: seen on mqtt.gomesh.dev and cross-checked against the",
    "  polygon-derived place of at least one located observer publishing under it.",
    "confidence=anticipated: an airport identifier inside a county in",
    "  the 1.1.0 boundary file, not yet observed on the broker. Listed so a",
    "  new gateway's coordinate-less observers land in a place instead of no region.",
    "Version 2 (1.2.0): `place` is a place code from the scope tree",
    "  (regions/us-ca-meshcore-scopes.json), never a county. Version 1 named a",
    "  `group` by display name; the server still reads that. San Joaquin North and",
    "  South codes now name the tree's single centralvalley."
  ],
